From b0900e6b3da61efeb79204a6c8c97be8f01d84a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anomalisfree <anomalisfree@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:13:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GS server patches: depth channel, depth loss, position
 anchor, aniso reg, photo-consistency tracking

Local changes made for the gs_server training pipeline, on top of upstream 3edecbb.
All new behavior is opt-in and off by default; with every new flag at its default, training
and the exported PLY are unchanged.

- Depth: 5th render output channel (view-space depth) in brush-render (forward + backward
  WGSL/Rust), per-view depth maps loaded from a sibling depth/ directory by brush-dataset,
  and --depth-loss-weight / --depth-max-range (readings beyond the cap are treated as
  missing; uncapped far LiDAR depth corrupted distant surfaces).
- Position anchor: --position-anchor-weight / --position-anchor-max-dist pull a splat toward
  the point-cloud position it (or its split ancestor) came from. Carried through prune and
  split/clone like the other per-splat tensors.
- Anisotropy regularization: --aniso-reg-weight / --aniso-reg-ratio-threshold penalize
  max/min scale ratio beyond a threshold.
- Photo-consistency tracking: --photo-consistency-enabled / --photo-consistency-warmup-steps
  accumulate per-splat render-vs-photo residual at the splat's projected pixel (read-only
  bookkeeping, never enters the loss) and export it as optional PLY properties
  photo_resid_avg / photo_resid_count. splat_to_ply gained an optional second argument.
- The penalty terms above are normalized by the count of violating splats, not all visible
  splats: a plain .sum() over ~1.7M splats either explodes (NaN) or is diluted to nothing.
- pred_rgb/gt_rgb are cloned in the lpips branch so later code can still use them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
